The '''M-68 landspeeder''' was a model of [[landspeeder]] manufactured by [[Mobquet Swoops and Speeders]]. A civilian model, the M-68 was popular among Corellian [[Racer|speeder enthusiasts]] due to the ease with which its [[repulsorlift generator]] could be modified and overcharged. It came in both a hard top and convertible configuration and had a [[duraplex]] windscreen.

An overpowered speeder of this type was stolen from [[Kilmo]] by [[Han Solo|Han]] on [[Corellia]], and later used by him and [[Qi'ra]] during their attempt to escape from the [[White Worms]], leading to a chase with [[Moloch]]'s [[A-A4B truckspeeder]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:M68landspeeder-SW100Objects.png|thumb|250px|right|Profile of a M-68 landspeeder]]
The M-68 was a compact civilian [[landspeeder]] model manufactured by [[Mobquet Swoops and Speeders]] and marketed to a youth audience. Available in both hardtop and open-air models, the M-68 was a high-performance vehicle powered by a [[289-hirep repulsorlift generator]] and two propulsion thrusters. Air was drawn into the speeder's custom cool-burning [[injectrine]] engines through the large, exposed inlet on the front grille. Each thruster had a variable exhaust nozzle that adjusted to shape and direct the thrust, allowing a [[pilot]] to spin the [[speeder]] at high speeds. The [[Repulsor field|repulsorfield]] also helped to generate better traction control, and was generated from transmitter banks between the rear-mounted thrusters.<ref name="Official Guide" /> The speeder featured air vents on the forward engine's front and dorsal surfaces to keep it cool,<ref name="Ultimate">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> including an exposed cooling fan fore of the windshield to cool the repulsorlift generator.<ref name="Official Guide" />

The speeder seated two, a pilot and passenger, behind its [[duraplex]] windshield,<ref name="ExplorerGuide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref> and featured a racing-style steering wheel with cut-out handles. A smooth spoiler behind the seats reduced air drag, and was fitted with an airspeed tracker and telemetry antenna. The vehicle's sides lacked the sleek finish of the chassis, instead exposing side ducting, fuel lines, and speed-governor mechanisms.<ref name="Official Guide" />

==History==
[[File:ChaseThruCoronet-SWBC56.png|left|thumb|250px|Han piloted a stolen M-68 on Corellia.]]
The M-68 was considered a classic by street racing enthusiasts,<ref name="Official Guide" /> who referred to it as a "street blaster bolt",<ref name="Ultimate" /> and particularly [[Corellian]] speeder enthusiasts.<ref name="Databank" /> Its 289-hirep could be easily modified and overcharged by thrill-seekers.<ref name="Official Guide" />

An overpowered,<ref name="Official Guide" /> street-racing-quality M-68 was owned by [[Kilmo]], brand-new as of his attempted [[coaxium]] deal with the [[scrumrat]] [[Han Solo|Han]] in [[Coronet City]] on [[Corellia]]. When the deal fell apart, Han fled and discovered the speeder, unprotected save for its security system. Han hid from his pursuers underneath the speeder,<ref name="Solo Expanded">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> and, recognizing its capabilities at a glance, employed a simple bit of hotwiring to steal it. He hung his set of [[aurodium]]-plated [[Han's dice|chance cubes]] from the landspeeder's windshield as a good luck charm.<ref name="Official Guide" /> Han drove it back to the [[Den of the White Worms]] where he later fled in the company of [[Qi'ra]] after an altercation with [[Lady]] [[Proxima]]. They were pursued by [[Moloch]] in his [[A-A4B truckspeeder]], and were forced to ditch the M-68 when Han attempted a maneuver that left it wedged between two buildings. He and Qi'ra escaped on foot to the [[Coronet City Spaceport|Coronet Spaceport]].<ref name="Solo" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:M68_Engines.png|thumb|right|250px|The shared engine part of the Halberd-441 and M-68 landspeeder]]
The M-68 landspeeder first appeared in the [[2018]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''. As shown in ''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', the [[Wikipedia:Dodge Charger|Dodge Charger]] automobile brand and the [[Wikipedia:Chevrolet Malibu|Chevrolet Malibu]] mid-size car model were early influences for the landspeeder.<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> The M-68 landspeeder used the same engine parts as [[Tayshin Maxa]] and [[Baroosh Pawk]]'s [[Halberd-441]] [[swoop]] bike, with a few modifications.<ref name="Heist">{{HomeVideoCite|film=Solo|featurette=The Train Heist}}</ref>

The vehicle was built by Lucasfilm's prop department. They used many "greebles" such as an aircraft's refueling hose. It was designed like a sports car, in comparison's to Moloch's speeder, which was designed after a truck.<ref name="Escape From Corellia">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'' "Escape From Corellia" Blu-Ray featurette</ref>

The speeder chase in the beginning of the film was a mixture of practical effects—a four-wheel drive vehicle—and CGI. Additionally, [[Skywalker Sound]] wanted to use real-world sounds to differentiate the speeders; part of the sound was recorded using homemade pulse-jet engines.<ref name="Escape From Corellia" />

